    "would enter the transcript and stay there, and tokens minted at runtime (session JWTs, ?token=…, signed URLs) are",
    "not masked by --secrets.",
    `Send it to a file in your scratch dir with the tool's own filename argument (an absolute path):`,
    `  ${short}({ …, filename: "${file.replace("~", home)}" })`,
    `(If the browser tool answers "File access denied", its MCP started before the per-seat dirs; until you relaunch, use`,
    `  ${legacyNetDir(home, env).replace(home, "~")}/${netKind(tool, ti)}-1.log instead.)`,
    `then print a summary that keeps method, host, path and status only (no query strings, no headers):`,
